From d5881f9d0af1b01e7dc18c051eda0b115dfa0a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:54:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Configuration codec: the edge-code language and its
 logspace decider

Adds the codes at radius s of window-bounded configurations with some work head at -s or s
(Codec/Langs: edgeLang, mem_edgeLang_iff), their word-level check with its characterization
(Codec/Checks: EdgeChk, edgeChk_def, getD_cfgWord_head, edgeChk_iff, edgeLang_iff), a fifth mode
edge of the codec machine that reads, tape by tape, the head flags of the first and last cells
(Codec/Machine: CMode.edge, its labels and loop sites, and the table at them as equations), and
its run and membership in L (Codec/Deciders: edge_round, edge_loop, edge_tail, edgeLang_mem).
Codec/Word gains W_eq and cellOf_head. The new proofs read the machine, the step and the
register files only through stated equations. No existing statement changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
